  "segments": [
    {
      "text": "For three generations, the families of Millbrook lived in the shadow of the Consolidated Chemical plant.",
      "startSeconds": 0,
      "durationSeconds": 6.925
    },
    {
      "text": "Cancer rates were 40% above the state average.",
      "startSeconds": 7.225,
      "durationSeconds": 3.925
    },
    {
      "text": "The river ran grey.",
      "startSeconds": 11.45,
      "durationSeconds": 1.9
    },
    {
      "text": "When 16-year-old Elena tested the tap water for her AP Environmental Science project and found lead levels exceeding EPA limits by a factor of three, something shifted.",
      "startSeconds": 13.65,
      "durationSeconds": 12.125
    },
    {
      "text": "\"We've been drinking this,\" she said, her voice barely above a whisper.",
      "startSeconds": 26.075,
      "durationSeconds": 4.475
    },
    {
      "text": "\"My little brother drinks this.\"",
      "startSeconds": 30.85,
      "durationSeconds": 2.25
    },
    {
      "text": "Elena's teacher, Dr. Parekh, connected her with researchers at State University who had documented successful community-led water remediation in Flint, Michigan, and Hinkley, California.",
      "startSeconds": 33.8,
      "durationSeconds": 13.15
    },
    {
      "text": "\"Change is possible,\" Dr. Parekh told her, \"but it requires evidence, organization, and persistence. Communities have won these fights before.\"",
      "startSeconds": 47.25,
      "durationSeconds": 9.75
    },
    {
      "text": "Elena and her classmates developed a comprehensive campaign.",
      "startSeconds": 57.7,
      "durationSeconds": 4.4
    },
    {
      "text": "They established a citizen science water testing network with standardized protocols.",
      "startSeconds": 62.4,
      "durationSeconds": 5.725
    },
    {
      "text": "They filed Freedom of Information requests for the plant's discharge records.",
      "startSeconds": 68.425,
      "durationSeconds": 5.1
    },
    {
      "text": "They partnered with the university's environmental law clinic to understand their legal options.",
      "startSeconds": 73.825,
      "durationSeconds": 6.3
    },
    {
      "text": "They created a public data dashboard showing real-time water quality readings.",
      "startSeconds": 80.425,
      "durationSeconds": 5.425
    },
    {
      "text": "The data dashboard went viral locally.",
      "startSeconds": 86.55,
      "durationSeconds": 3.075
    },
    {
      "text": "Within six months, the state environmental agency launched a formal investigation.",
      "startSeconds": 89.925,
      "durationSeconds": 6.35
    },
    {
      "text": "The plant was fined $2.4 million and required to install new filtration systems.",
      "startSeconds": 96.575,
      "durationSeconds": 6.675
    },
    {
      "text": "Elena testified before the state legislature about the importance of environmental monitoring in underserved communities.",
      "startSeconds": 103.55,
      "durationSeconds": 8.55
    },
    {
      "text": "A new community water treatment facility was funded through a combination of the fine revenue and a federal environmental justice grant.",
      "startSeconds": 112.4,
      "durationSeconds": 9.125
    }
  ],
